From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:19:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 173/177] fix(gastown): polecat claim guards molecule roots,
 checks unknown reasons, retries non-object output (gcp-x8jue, gcp-4b7ji)

Three defects in the polecat claim, fixed in one commit because two of them
rewrite the same live-owner trigger line.

gcp-x8jue: the live-owner guard ran only when the claimed bead carried
gc.step_ref. A mol-polecat-work ROOT carries gc.kind=workflow and gc.step_id but
neither gc.step_ref nor gc.root_bead_id, and the pool offers a root as a launch
fallback once no step is ready, which is the state a controller restart leaves a
live molecule in. A claim landing on a root therefore skipped the guard and
reported ownership while another live session held the molecule's steps (winnow
04:38Z: capable claimed a root while nux held self-review). The guard now also
triggers on gc.step_id or gc.kind=workflow, and a workflow bead with no
gc.root_bead_id is its own GUARD_ROOT, so the last holder comes from its steps.
The two new derivations sit inside the GUARD_BEGIN/END sentinels because the
guard-extracting tests bind only STEP_REF and SHOW_JSON.

gcp-4b7ji #1: the comment said an unknown hook reason still checks, but the code
skipped every reason except claimed and empty. The guard now skips exactly
existing_assignment and ready_assignment, which prove the bead carried our
identity before the hook ran; every other reason checks. Wrongly checking costs
two or three gc calls; wrongly skipping stomps a live worktree.

gcp-4b7ji #2: the comment said malformed output is retried, but stdout that was
not a JSON object at exit 0 fell through to NO_ROUTED_WORK and drained. gc
writes exactly one object per call, so anything else is a truncated or corrupted
result, possibly of a claim gc already won; the retry gets that bead back as
existing_assignment where draining would park it. Empty stdout and {} stay
NO_ROUTED_WORK.

Tests: the ok_hook fixture now uses the real success shape (action "work"),
test_case_unknownrsn and test_case_garbage are rewritten to the new behaviour,
and nine cases are added (rootlive, roottag, rootdead, rootfresh, garbageflaky,
nonobject, existing, rootexisting, blank), 28 -> 37. Every new behavioural case
fails against the old script; existing, rootexisting and blank pin the paths
that must not change. The prompt template is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-claim.sh |  49 ++++-
